  "id": "BIT-nginx-gateway-2026-120967",
  "summary": "NGINX ngx_stream_ssl_module vulnerability",
  "details": "When NGINX Plus or NGINX Open Source is configured to require client certificates (\"ssl_verify_client on\") in a non-default stream virtual server, a remote attacker could bypass verification of client certificates.\n\nImpact:\nAn attacker could leverage this vulnerability to bypass verification of client certificates. There is no control plane exposure; this is a data plane issue only.\n\n\n\nNote: Software versions which have reached End of Technical Support (EoTS) are not evaluated.",
